// error
// #4137: `isBytesConversion` (lowerlit.bit) admitted the §12.9 `[]byte(s)`
// bytes-conversion early return on a single `string` argument alone, with no
// check that the slice's element is byte-sized — unlike the checker's own
// `vSliceAllocIsBytesForm` (validatezero.bit), which requires both. `bit
// check`/`build`/`run` never reached the gap (this fixture's own E0111 is
// what stops them), but `--dump-ir`/`--dump-ir-pre` lower unchecked input
// (#3756) and took the bytes-conversion path regardless of element type:
// `[]i64("hello")` lowered to `rt_call bytes_from_string(...) []i64` — a
// 5-byte buffer typed as a 5-element `[]i64`, reading past the allocation for
// any index beyond 0. This fixture is the regression guard for the exact
// reported form so it can never silently return.
fn main() {
  let xs = []i64("hello")
  print("${len(xs)}\n")
}
